# Netlify redirect rules for the Web.Client SPA.
# Lives in public/ so Vite copies it into dist/ (the Netlify publish directory).
# Rules are processed top-down, first match wins, and before netlify.toml.

# --- Optional: same-origin API proxy (disabled by default) ---
# Uncommenting this makes Netlify proxy /api/* to the .NET API server-side, so
# every request is same-origin. CORS then stops applying entirely and
# VITE_API_URL can stay unset -- api.ts falls back to baseURL "/api", which
# mirrors the dev proxy in vite.config.ts.
#
# WARNING: Netlify proxy rewrites time out after 26 seconds. The dev API runs on
# Render's free plan, which spins down when idle, and Program.cs runs EF
# migrations + DbInitializer before serving traffic. A cold start can exceed 26s
# and return a gateway error. Only enable this once the API is on a paid plan or
# is kept warm.
#
# /api/*  https://dotnet-questionnaire-vfbsac-nbtr.onrender.com/:splat  200

# SPA fallback: serve index.html for client-side routes, so a hard reload or a
# shared deep link (/admin/specialities, /form/:id, ...) does not 404.
# Must stay last -- /* matches everything.
/*  /index.html  200
